Z||000003||Dan010||12-24-2001||12:30 AM||||Visually looking at the TCV cable it looks fine. have not pulled it out of the trans.<BR>Throttle body end is fine.  Took it in to trans shop, they serviced it, asked them to check and adjust TCV cable. The service tech<BR>said the shift point was fine in his opinion.<BR>How does one check for sticky valve body??<BR>If I adjust the TCV cable so shifting is harder, what will the cause and effect be??<BR>This is not a racer, just want it to everything to work the best that it can, realizing the age of this car. It may be just fine as is. Just never owned or driven any other Fiero.<BR> Drove my van today, and paid attention for the first time of its shift points, seems to be about the same kick down speed to first gear. Could be everything is perfect as is!!!<BR>Thank You||||reg||1
